{
  "hypothesis": "Under uniform circuit-level depolarizing noise at p = 1e-3, decoded logical teleportation failure of an XX lattice-surgery protocol between two rotated surface-code patches falls by a factor Lambda >= 2 at each distance step d = 3 to 5 and d = 5 to 7. Rounds of initialization and of the merge both equal d. Lambda is the ratio of seed-means of p_bar(d) = (p_fail_Z(d) + p_fail_X(d)) / 2 over seeds 0, 1 and 2. p_fail_b is the fraction of shots on which PyMatching disagrees with the sampled observable in basis b. This is a stim simulation of the protocol, not a re-run of the 41-qubit device in arXiv:2611.23165.\n",
